      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A 12V compressor fridge for a cabin or narrowboat draws 30 to 50 W when the compressor runs and nothing when the thermostat is satisfied. Average draw for a 50-litre fridge in a 20 degrees Celsius ambient: about 0.4 to 0.6 Ah per hour. An absorption refrigeration fridge on LPG uses around 180 to 250 g of LPG per day for the same 50-litre box. At UK LPG bulk prices, that is roughly 0.30 to 0.45 pounds per day.",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "12V compressor fridge advantages",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Higher ",
                    "type": "text"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "COP",
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termId": "cmpv497sa0000mkv4910l3m20"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ": more cooling per unit of energy. If the energy is solar, this matters.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Better in hot weather: above 25 degrees Celsius, absorption fridges lose cooling capacity fast. Compressor fridges hold their performance.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Works on any angle: suitable for vehicles and boats.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "No gas: eliminates LPG supply logistics and fire risk.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Gas absorption fridge advantages",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "No electricity needed on LPG: the right choice for a cabin with no solar and little battery storage.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "No moving parts: theoretically infinite service life. A well-maintained absorption fridge lasts 30 to 40 years.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Silent operation: no compressor noise.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Multi-fuel: most absorption fridges run on LPG, 230V, or 12V. Easy to switch between power sources.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The decision",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For a cabin with a 400 Wp solar array and a 200 Ah lithium battery: a 12V compressor fridge draws 12 to 15 Ah per day in cool weather. The solar array will cover this easily in summer and on bright winter days. For a property with no solar and grid connection only by generator: a gas absorption fridge on LPG with 12V backup is more practical. For a narrowboat that is frequently blacked out and heated by diesel: LPG is already on board. An absorption fridge running on LPG eliminates the 12V load.",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "title": "Troubleshooter"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Gas absorption fridge not cooling despite gas burning"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "The boiler tube may have residue blocking it, or the ammonia solution may have migrated. Invert the fridge for 4 hours then return it to upright and reconnect the gas. This redistributes the ammonia. If it still does not cool, the boiler tube needs cleaning by a qualified engineer or replacement.",
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
